<title>UK: UK Q3 1996 GDP rises final 0.7 percent q/q.</title>
<headline>UK Q3 1996 GDP rises final 0.7 percent q/q.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following gross domestic product data for Q3 1996. GDP (FACTOR COST, 1990 PRICES)</p>
<p>			    Q3,96	   Q2,96	   Q3,95</p>
<p>    Index		 108.9 (108.9) 108.2 (108.1) 106.4(106.4)</p>
<p>    pct change q/q	0.7 (0.8)     0.6 (0.5)   0.6</p>
<p>    pct change y/y	2.4 (2.4)     2.3 (2.2)   2.2</p>
<p>GDP AT MARKET PRICES (MONEY GDP)</p>
<p>    Index		 134.4	   132.7	   127.6</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr   1.3	   n/a	     n/a</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr    5.3	   n/a	     n/a</p>
<p>GDP EX OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION (CONSTANT PRICES)</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr   0.7	    0.5	     0.5</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr    2.3	    2.1	     2.1</p>
<p>PERSONAL SECTOR INCOME, SPENDING, SAVING</p>
<p>					    (million stg) QQ%	YY%</p>
<p> Total personal pre-tax income    167,954   1.0	6.0</p>
<p> Wages,salaries,forces pay	   86,865   1.2	4.4</p>
<p> Total personal disposable income 134,993   1.4	7.5</p>
<p>Consumer expenditure (current  market prices)			 119,169   1.6	6.1</p>
<p>  Real personal disposable income 106,499   0.8	4.6</p>
<p>	 (% change QQ)		  Q3	  Q2	 Q3/Q3 95</p>
<p>  Expenditure deflator		0.7	 n/a	2.8</p>
<p>Implied GDP deflator (at   factor cost)			  1.1	 n/a	3.2</p>
<p>Consumer spending (constant   1990 prices)			  1.0	 n/a	3.2</p>
<p>					    Q3	  Q2	 Q3 95</p>
<p>  Personal saving (million stg)	 15,824    15,842   13,163</p>
<p>  Savings ratio (pct)		 11.7	11.9     10.5</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of economists found a consensus expecting Q3 GDP growth to be unrevised at 0.8 percent on the quarter and 2.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>The ONS said some back data was not published due to delays caused by the recent fire in the Treasury building.</p>
</text>
